# spinnerdemo: the Spinner widget (line preset, 100ms fps) driving Tea v2's
# tick re-arm under a real pty.
# Frame trace (each repaint is ONE write; first paint hides the cursor):
#   resize probe (sync)  \e[?25l\e[2K|\r\n
#   tick 1 (sleep 100)   \e[1A\e[2K/\r\n
#   tick 2 (re-armed)    \e[1A\e[2K-\r\n
#   'q'                  \e[?25h + exit 0  (TaskQuit scan; the pending sleep
#                         is dropped by the quit latch)
# Frames cycle | / - \ every ~100ms, so needles span a frame BOUNDARY (prev
# frame's tail \r\n -> next frame's \e[1A\e[2K<char>): such a substring cannot
# exist until the NEXT frame is actually written, making every expect
# deterministic regardless of tick timing (R4: never assert tick counts).
expect \e[?25l
expect |\r\n\e[1A\e[2K/
expect /\r\n\e[1A\e[2K-
send q
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
